  "name": "clarkson-cs470",
  "description": "This repository centralizes coursework and project-based implementations for a machine learning curriculum, focusing on both supervised and unsupervised neural architectures. The codebase features robust data pipelines for financial fraud detection, employing one-hot vectorization, min-max normalization, and temporal partitioning on high-cardinality imbalanced datasets. It further implements foundational computer vision models including CNNs and U-Nets for semantic segmentation, alongside exploratory clustering analysis using k-Means and the elbow method.",
